[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=Gaming Setup
GenericName=GE-Proton for Steam
Comment=Download a community GE-Proton build for Steam; compatibility varies by game
Exec=konsole -e sh -c '/usr/bin/dagric-gaming ; echo ; printf "Press Enter to close..." ; read x'
Icon=dagric-gaming
Terminal=false
Categories=Game;System;
Keywords=steam;proton;ge-proton;proton-ge;wine;gaming;game;compatibility;performance;gamemode;mangohud;
# NO X-Dagric-Edition FLAG HERE, DELIBERATELY — the omission IS the fix.
#
# This file used to carry the Pro flag, and 0510-app-names.hook.chroot (plus
# dagric-app-names, which re-runs after every apt operation) DELETES every file
# carrying it from a free image. So free had no "Gaming Setup" entry at all,
# while the manual page for this helper is marked data-avail="free" and tells
# its owner in as many words: launcher -> Gaming Setup. Sending a free owner to
# a menu entry the build removed is the "free edition reads as BROKEN" failure
# this project forbids.
#
# It is not a Pro tool. /usr/bin/dagric-gaming ships on both editions, the Hub
# offers its row on both, and by the rule in docs/EDITIONS.md a helper that only
# FETCHES something free — GE-Proton, a community Proton build — is not a gate.
# The two genuinely Pro launcher entries are dagric-usb-protect and dagric-vm.

